anoma. Patient remains in stable condition with no evidence of disease progression. Physical examination and vital signs were within normal limits.\n\nOverall, Katie Coleman has been compliant with her follow-up care and her stage III malignant melanoma is currently controlled with no evidence of disease progression. She has a history of tobacco use but successfully quit in March 2025. Her most recent visit was for a rash, which was evaluated and treated accordingly.\n"
